from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;j=json.loads((R/'results.json').read_text())
labels={'both_events':'Two fresh events agree','stoch_event_sma_state':'Stochastic event + SMA direction','sma_event_stoch_state':'SMA crossover + stochastic direction','stoch_event_two_sma_states':'Stochastic event + two SMA directions'}
def pct(v):return '—' if v is None else f'{100*v:.2f}%'
def row(c,selected=False):
 m=c['final_reused'];ci=c['bootstrap'];anchor=j['baselines'][c['anchor']]
 vals=[labels[c['recipe']],'<br>'.join(html.escape(k) for k in c['components']),pct(anchor['accuracy']),pct(m['accuracy']),str(m['active']),f"{m['correlation']:.4f}",('—' if ci is None else pct(ci['accuracy_95'][0])+'–'+pct(ci['accuracy_95'][1]))]
 return '<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+v+'</td>' for v in vals)+'</tr>'
chosen=[next(c for c in j['candidates'] if c['id']==v) for k,v in j['selection'].items() if k!='overall' and v]
allrows=''.join(row(c) for c in sorted(j['candidates'],key=lambda c:c['validation']['correlation'],reverse=True))
best=max((c for c in j['candidates'] if c['final_reused']['active']>=100),key=lambda c:c['final_reused']['accuracy'])
header='<tr>'+''.join('<th>'+s+'</th>' for s in ['Recipe','Components','Anchor alone','Combined accuracy','Signals','Correlation','95% accuracy interval'])+'</tr>'
body='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>BTC stochastic + SMA research</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:1250px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 22px;color:#203046}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd}td:nth-child(2){max-width:330px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.lead{background:#edf2f7;padding:20px;border-radius:12px}</style></head><body><h1>Stochastic + SMA confirmation</h1><p>October 18, 2026 · Kalshi BTC 15-minute outcomes · 90 fixed combinations</p><p class="lead"><b>No reliable improvement established.</b> The overall validation-selected model was the 5m stochastic (48,5,5) crossover confirmed by the 5m SMA 2/5 direction. Final accuracy increased from 51.87% (455 signals) to 52.59% (367 signals), a gain of 0.72 percentage points. The paired daily-block 95% interval for that gain is −1.38 to +3.09 points. Correlation increased from 0.0139 to 0.0174; its improvement interval also includes zero.</p><h2>Validation-selected winner in each recipe</h2><table>'''+header+''.join(row(c) for c in chosen)+'''</table><p>The two-event combination retained only 228 of the 15m stochastic turn's 995 signals and scored 53.51%, versus 53.57% alone. Confirming the 15m SMA5/10 crossover with the 5m stochastic direction scored 52.46%, versus 52.54% alone. Adding two SMA chart confirmations did not produce a reliable advantage either.</p><h2>What was combined</h2><p>Stochastic parameters were frozen to the preceding validation selections: 5m (48,5,5) K/D crossover; 15m (5,1,1) K turning up from ≤20 or down from ≥80; 30m (8,3,1) with the same turn rule. SMA lengths were 2/5 and 5/10 candles, each on 5m, 15m and 30m charts.</p><p>All 18 stochastic-chart × SMA-chart × SMA-pair assignments were tested for each of three two-indicator recipes, plus 36 stochastic-event confirmations using SMA states on two different charts. All inputs must agree. A direction state is not a new crossover: stochastic state means K-D sign for the 5m family and K-slope sign for the turn families; SMA state means fast above/below slow. These controls are explicitly distinct from simultaneous events.</p><h2>Exploratory high score—not the selected winner</h2><p>After looking across the final-period results, the highest accuracy among combinations with at least 100 signals was '''+pct(best['final_reused']['accuracy'])+' across '+str(best['final_reused']['active'])+' signals: '+html.escape(', '.join(best['components']))+'''. This was found by inspecting the evaluation results and is not independent evidence of an edge. It was not the validation-selected winner and should not be substituted for it. It needs a new prospective test.</p><h2>Evaluation boundaries</h2><p>Reused 17,027 official Kalshi outcomes from April 21–October 17 UTC and the same Coinbase BTC-USD candles. Final evaluation: September 13–October 17 UTC, 3,320 markets. This period was inspected in earlier studies; results are exploratory, not fresh holdout evidence. The models were locked before this run's final metrics, but their component choices inherit earlier research exposure.</p><p>Signals use only completed bars at quarter-hour market starts. Events between starts are not carried forward; chart states may be. A 30m event only triggers at alternate starts. Missing windows are excluded. Entry-time availability, asks, spreads, fees, depth and fills are unmodeled; there is no net-profit claim.</p><p>Selection required at least 200 training and 100 validation signals and ranked validation correlation. Final intervals use 2,000 daily-block resamples and are not multiple-comparison-adjusted. Signals below 100 final occurrences are sparse. Agreement filters retain the same directional predictions as their components on overlapping trades; their effect is selection of opportunities, not a new independent prediction on those trades. The paired comparisons use the same valid market universe, while the traded subsets differ.</p><p>Verification: five focused tests, independent scalar agreement/count/accuracy/correlation checks for all 90 combinations, all 15 prior event/SMA-state baseline matches, and five validation-selection checks. No trading services, accounts or rules changed.</p><details><summary>All 90 combinations, sorted by validation correlation</summary><table>'''+header+allrows+'''</table></details><p>Reproducible artifacts: EXPERIMENT.md, study.py, selection-lock.json, results.json, final-predictions.csv, verification.json. Canonical report proof: cloud-record.json.</p></body></html>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(body)
(R/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({p.name:hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in R.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name not in ('manifest.json','run.log')},indent=2))
